report.summary:
I updated docs/jit-guide.md and docs/roadmap.md for the select fix. README.md needed no change: it still says twelve patch scripts and never mentions select. I wrote nothing under native/ or test/. The implementer's four files have the md5s their report gives (patch b218585d, run-bitjit 01cc9a17, negctl 4affc917, t_select b2616108).

Roadmap row 213 is now marked [x] and holds, as one line: the exact input, the mechanism (three classes of k plus the constant path's C overflow), the fix, the tests, the arms, the checks with their paths, upstream's status at dd3b243, and what is left open. The row states plainly that the full 32-arm negctl sweep, the smoke timing and the release natives had not run when it was written; it names bench/runs/2026-10-21-select/ (logs/final-main/, logs/release/, scripts/, design/) as the evidence home. The sweep's unfixed findings went into a new row at line 214, so rows 1-213 keep their lines. The upstream-reports row gained a fourth candidate, and row 211 (5) is now marked as the next round.

In the guide, P54 is now the record of the fix and keeps its number. The Next task is (1) FIX-NUMCONV, then (2) row 209's loop-carried widths. I added:
- section 11.5b for the sel part;
- P59, the hot-counter penalty flake;
- 8.6 step 7, so a guard's own arithmetic cannot wrap;
- a note in 8.5 on record-time C overflow;
- narrowing's wrapped index in 3.13.

I also updated 1.2, 2.5, 2.6, 7.5, 8.2, 8.8, 9.6, 9.8, 11, 11.2, 11.3, 11.7, 11.8, 11.9, 11.11, 12.10, Appendix A, the glossary and open question 19.

The patch moves no LuaJIT line cite in the guide, because every lj_record.c cite there is a pristine one. The cites into run-bitjit.sh and negctl-bitop.sh were moved with a difflib map and checked by content: 86 cites hold. Moved by one line, 85 of them fail moving down and all 86 fail moving up.

Final md5s: docs/jit-guide.md 7a83664d0c33df10996055eaf1ed358d (HEAD 73f87849), docs/roadmap.md c033426940d706d78d25e9813cb70e6c (HEAD 2f4c5c07), README.md 98f6042d7386c9b999ea709d9c5889d7 (unchanged). Both docs have 0 CR and 0 TAB bytes, and git diff --check is clean.

One rule slip: a single read-only command of mine ran `python -` (P53) and had a backslash in its text (P8). I stopped it with TaskStop; it wrote nothing, and I redid it with a script file.

findings:
docs/roadmap.md row 213 (line 213, still one line). Marked [x] and retitled 'returned nil ... fixed in our fork the same day (JIT guide P54 and 11.5b)'. It covers:
- the input: 7 varargs; K[i]=100 records path C; K[150]=-2147483628; the JIT prints 'n 30 E 200' where -joff prints 'E 30 E 200';
- the mechanism: paths A, B and C, and three classes of k: an 8k wrap; k in m+1..0 when there are fewer arguments than fixed parameters; a narrowing-wrapped k;
- the fix, hunks 4 and 5 in patch-bitop-record.sh, with the reason penalty-scrub was not used;
- the constant path's C overflow (LT fr, -2147483621; 26 trace starts);
- k >= 2^28, t_select and the sel part, the arms (SELGUARD 11-53, SELRECK 2-3 of 3, four runs), the checks with paths, and upstream at dd3b243;
- open items: keep SELRECK or not; t_idx2's and twin.lua's headers; the KMAX choice; the next row.
It says the full sweep, the timing and the release had not run at writing.

